From ddca15864891277164049b7b4c4a7fd64e392a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:02:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 101/105] test: add script tests for P2MR leaf version 0xe2

150 rows of script_tests.json, made by the new
test/util/generate_p2mr_lattice_tripwire_script_tests.py with real
Schnorr, ML-DSA-44 and SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s signatures over the transactions
script_json_test builds, as the rows of leaf version 0xe0 are. They go
above the rows of leaf version 0xe0, where no other generator rewrites
them. They cover the combinations of P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE,
P2MR_EC_DISABLED and P2MR_MLDSA_DISABLED:

- without P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE a leaf of version 0xe2 at depth one is not
  executed, whatever else is set, and is discouraged as an upgradable
  leaf version;
- with it and no check disabled, S1, a Schnorr leaf, S2, SLH1 and an
  ML-DSA-44 AND SLH-DSA leaf behave as in leaf version 0xc0;
- with P2MR_EC_DISABLED, the elliptic curve checks fail as in 0xe0: the
  rows of leaf version 0xe0 again, with P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE alone, with
  P2MR_EC_DISABLED and with both disabled (OP_CHECKSIG, OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY
  and OP_CHECKSIGADD with valid, invalid and empty signatures; signatures
  of 63 and 520 bytes and a 521-byte push; an explicit SIGHASH_DEFAULT
  byte and hash type 0x04; an empty, a 32-byte and a 33-byte public key;
  OP_NOT after a check; a 5-byte number before OP_CHECKSIGADD; validation
  weight used up just before the check, or not);
- with P2MR_MLDSA_DISABLED, any non-empty signature fails as disabled,
  valid or not, whatever its chunk sizes and hash type, with OP_NOT after
  it too; a 521-byte chunk still fails before the script runs, seven
  stack elements, a public key chunk of 519 bytes and a budget short by
  one still fail first; an empty signature still pushes false; SLH1 and
  leaf versions 0xc0 and 0xe0 are not affected;
- with both, S2 and the AND leaf fail as disabled and SLH1 passes;
- ML-DSA-44, Schnorr and SLH-DSA signatures do not carry over between
  leaf versions 0xc0, 0xe0 and 0xe2, in either direction;
  a lone leaf of version 0xe2 is at depth zero and never executed; control
  byte 0xe2 is refused; in P2TR leaf version 0xe2 stays unknown.

Every row passes the random flag changes of script_json_test: passing rows
list no DISCOURAGE flag that would turn a removed execution flag into a
failure, and a row that fails only because P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE is absent
carries a witness that fails once the leaf executes. The
DeferringSignatureChecker check of script_json_test runs on each.
